<div class="sop-meta">
  <div><strong>Trigger</strong> Client gives 30-day notice (per agreement) or moves to a different vendor</div>
  <div><strong>Owner</strong> Primary owner</div>
  <div><strong>Time</strong> 2-5 hours of work spread across the 30-day window</div>
  <div><strong>Output</strong> Clean handoff. Client keeps domain, content, and (on lump-sum) code. We keep our reputation.</div>
</div>

<h2>Posture</h2>
<p>We don't hold domains, content, or accounts hostage. Period. The day a client says "I want to leave," we move into helpful-handoff mode. The relationship and our reputation are worth more than the last invoice.</p>

<h2>Steps</h2>

<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Acknowledge the notice within 1 business hour. No guilt, no defensiveness, no last-ditch save attempt.</li>
  <li>Confirm the official end date (30 days from notice for monthly clients).</li>
  <li>Schedule a 20-minute exit call within 5 business days.</li>
  <li>On the call: ask why (genuinely). Listen. Don't argue. Sometimes there's something we should fix; sometimes it's just a fit issue.</li>
  <li>Walk through the handoff checklist together (below).</li>
  <li>Send the handoff email same day with the bundle attached.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The handoff bundle</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Domain:</strong> already at their registrar in their name. We just unlink from our hosting. Provide written confirmation: "DNS pointed away from us as of {date}."</li>
  <li><strong>Content:</strong> exported as a clean HTML/Markdown bundle. Include all media files. Zip it; send via Drive or Dropbox.</li>
  <li><strong>Code (Lump-Sum clients):</strong> already theirs. Transfer the GitHub repo to their account or a new account they create.</li>
  <li><strong>Code (Monthly clients):</strong> we own the code per the agreement. Provide a static export of the live site (HTML/CSS/JS) that runs on any host with no dependencies. Can re-host the export anywhere. We don't transfer the repo.</li>
  <li><strong>Forms:</strong> the Web3Forms account is in their name (or transferable in one email). Walk them through.</li>
  <li><strong>Email:</strong> already theirs (we never had control). Confirm.</li>
  <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> Cloudflare Web Analytics dashboard exports last 90 days as CSV. Umami dashboard credentials transferred or revoked per their preference.</li>
  <li><strong>Search Console:</strong> they own the verified property; we just remove our user access.</li>
  <li><strong>Brand assets / logos / photos:</strong> all theirs. Confirmation note.</li>
</ul>

