<h2>Internal cleanup (within 7 days of end_date)</h2>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Remove client from active-clients spreadsheet; move to "former clients" sheet with end date + reason.</li>
  <li>Cancel Cloudflare Pages project (after confirming DNS is pointed elsewhere).</li>
  <li>Archive the GitHub repo (private; mark as archived but don't delete).</li>
  <li>Archive the Drive folder (move to "archive/{client}").</li>
  <li>Stop billing.</li>
  <li>Stop uptime monitoring on their domain.</li>
  <li>Remove from WHOIS-watch list.</li>
  <li>Note in CRM: end date, reason, anything to learn from.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Common offboarding issues</h2>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>Client says they want to leave but doesn't follow up</strong>
  Don't push them out. Send a 1-week check-in: "Still planning to move? Either way is fine; just want to plan the handoff." Sometimes people change their mind.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>Client wants to leave but doesn't have a new vendor lined up</strong>
  Help them shop. Ask what they're looking for. Recommend specific people if you know any. Don't trash-talk our competitors.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>Client wants to take the Monthly-plan code (not just a static export)</strong>
  Per the agreement, we own the source on Monthly. Offer a code-buyout: typically a one-time fee equal to 6 months of plan + a clean transfer. Document if they accept.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>Client wants to dispute the last month's bill on the way out</strong>
  Refund or pro-rate per the agreement, no argument. The relationship is over either way; don't burn the last bridge over $175.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout">
  <strong>Client wants to come back later</strong>
  Welcome them back. Restart fees apply per the agreement (typically equivalent to the initial onboarding effort). Document the gap and reset the 12-month minimum.
</div>

<h2>Exit criteria</h2>
<p>Handoff bundle delivered, internal cleanup complete, client confirmed they have everything. Move them to the former-clients sheet. Stay polite if they reach out later for advice; we don't ghost.</p>
